          <caption>
            <p>Noncardiogenic Pulmonary Edema, Chest Radiograph. A classic batwing pattern of pulmonary opacities is observed. Cardiomegaly, vascular redistribution, pleural effusion, septal lines, and mediastinal widening are usually absent. A patchy distribution of edema with air bronchograms and peripheral ground-glass opacities may also be present. Contributed by&#x000a0;S Bhimji, MD</p>
          </caption>
          <graphic xmlns:xlink="http://www.w3.org/1999/xlink" xlink:href="Noncardiogenic__pul__edema" position="float" orientation="portrait"/>
